  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Food lowers absorption, cutting peak levels by 29 to 53%. It is 97% protein bound and predominantly metabolised by CYP3A4.",
    "substance": "A cyclic compound with a molecular weight of 1214.6 g/mole, which appears as a solid.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as 7.9 mg capsules, dosed twice daily.",
    "safety": "Boxed warning for malignancies and serious infections; contraindicated with strong CYP3A4 inhibitors and with hypersensitivity to any excipient. Decreased glomerular filtration rate is among the common adverse reactions.",
    "indication": "Adults with active lupus nephritis, given with a background immunosuppressive regimen.",
    "mechanism": "Suppresses calcineurin, a step in lymphocyte activation, reducing lymphocyte proliferation and T-cell cytokine production."
  },
  "tell": "A calcineurin inhibitor whose whole-blood exposure rises more than dose-proportionally across its therapeutic range.",
